# WASM Compatibility Constraints

All crates in this repo (except `pf_test_harness`) must compile to `wasm32-wasi`.

## Forbidden patterns

- `tokio::runtime::Runtime` or any full tokio runtime — use Spin SDK async
- `std::net::TcpStream` / `std::net::UdpSocket` — use `spin_sdk::http`
- `std::fs::*` — use Spin key-value store or external storage
- `std::process::Command` — not available in WASM
- `libc` or `nix` crate — native-only
- `reqwest` with default features — use `spin_sdk::http::send` or WASM-compatible HTTP

## Allowed patterns

- `spin_sdk::*` for all I/O (HTTP, key-value, SQLite, variables)
- `serde` / `serde_json` for serialization
- Pure computation crates (no I/O)
- Template engines: Sailfish, Askama, MiniJinja (all WASM-compatible)

## Exceptions

- `pf_test_harness` — native-only test crate, may use tokio/axum
- `examples/a2a-echo-native` — native example

## Quick check

```bash
cargo check --target wasm32-wasi -p <crate-name>
```
